l/pyproject is found — a deleted temp dir root yields defaults (direct-Anthropic + fallback), not an error","The whole point (Context) is that the direct-Anthropic fallback is what collapsed prompt_cache_style to none and doubled review cost"],"finding":"The parity guarantee depends on the ephemeral tempfile.mkdtemp() config_root surviving until a LATER Tier-1/Tier-2 ticket constructs LLMConfig(repo_path=pinned.config_root); the plan specifies no lifecycle/ownership for that temp dir. If it is removed or GC'd before the eval call, _discover_project_config finds no rebar.toml, read_reserved_section degrades to {}, and load_class_slots returns built-in DIRECT-ANTHROPIC defaults WITH a fallback — silently re-introducing the mixed-chain/cache-collapse hazard the ticket exists to prevent, rather than failing loud.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f622bd3ffeea5c241","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Pinned targets, with a GENUINELY homogeneous chain' (resolve_pinned_model returns PinnedModel(config_root: str) pointing at tempfile.mkdtemp())","norm_id":"n3ab33da3e208f6cc","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Tier-1 ticket calls resolve_pinned_model, then the temp dir is cleaned (e.g. TemporaryDirectory context exit, OS /tmp reaping, or a separate process) before the eval run builds its LLMConfig","A test or caller reuses config_root across process boundaries"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artif